      passage: `The founding of Grammar Keep required each of the three Scholar-clans to relinquish something precious. The Grammarians gave up exclusive control over language standards. The Logicians gave up the claim that their discipline was primary. The Rhetoricians gave up the most — their independence, their reputation for persuasive cunning, their image as the Keep's most sophisticated thinkers.`,
