      pre_narrative: `"The underlined transition in this passage is wrong," the Irrelevant Lord announces. "Or is it? Mwahaha. Also, I lied — it is wrong. But only subtly. You must read the entire paragraph to see why."`,
      passage: `Warden Callus began his educational reform by eliminating multiple-choice grammar tests. He replaced them with open-ended questions that required students to explain why a sentence was correct or incorrect. Student performance initially dropped — the new format was harder. [However], students who completed two semesters under the new system showed dramatically higher scores on complex writing assessments than their predecessors had.`,
