      passage: `The Grammar Council's official history presents the founding of Grammar Keep as a triumph of scholarly cooperation. This account has never been seriously challenged — not because it is accurate, but because challenging it requires access to primary documents that the Council controls. The primary documents, when accessed by independent researchers, tell a different story: negotiations were bitter, the founding charter went through forty-seven drafts, and two of the three clan leaders signed only under significant political pressure. [______], the official history is not a neutral record but an institutionally maintained myth.`,
      question_stem: `Which transition word or phrase best fills the blank in the paragraph above?`,
