      type: 'boss',
      difficulty: 3,
      enemy_name: 'The Irrelevant Lord',
      enemy_type: 'Rhetoric Warden',
      pre_narrative: `"This transition question has a trap," the Lord says, almost admiringly. "One of the answer options is tempting because it is not wrong — just less precise than the correct answer. Also, I respect precision. Not enough to practice it. But enough to respect it in others. Proceed."`,
      passage: `Warden Holt's compromise ruling on the serial comma was initially dismissed by both sides. [______], by the end of the Fifth Age, the compromise had become the operative standard across all but two of the Keep's districts, not because either faction had been persuaded of its philosophical merit, but because it worked in practice.`,
