      pre_narrative: `"Word choice!" the Irrelevant Lord snarls. "Three of these. I find word choice questions personally offensive. Every word should mean approximately whatever the reader wants it to mean. Also, imprecision is my third favorite thing, after irrelevance and disorder. Now. Choose your word carefully."`,
      passage: `The Grammar Council's handling of the Comma Plague was widely praised in official accounts. Independent scholars, however, have [______] that the Council's slow initial response allowed the Plague to spread to districts that might have been protected by earlier intervention.`,
      question_stem: `Which of the following most precisely expresses the writer's intended meaning in the blank?`,
