      pre_narrative: `"Tone question!" the Irrelevant Lord announces. "My least favorite, because tone is something I have never possessed. Also, I once attempted a solemn tone in a speech and accidentally made everyone laugh. Irrelevant! This passage is from the Keep's founding philosophical treatise. One sentence breaks the register."`,
      passage: `The founding scholars understood that institutions, like arguments, must be built from the ground up. Every structural element must be justified by the principles it embodies, not by tradition or convenience. An institution that cannot explain why it does what it does is not an institution — it is a habit. You really have to hand it to them for figuring all this out. The founding charter was, in this sense, not merely a legal document but a philosophical proof: evidence that an institution built on explicit principles could exist.`,
