      difficulty: 3,
      enemy_name: 'The Irrelevant Lord',
      enemy_type: 'Rhetoric Warden',
      pre_narrative: `"The final word choice question," the Irrelevant Lord says, and his voice drops to something that might almost be called respect. "This one is the hardest. The difference between the correct answer and the wrong answer is a single degree of precision. I genuinely do not expect you to get this right."`,
      passage: `The Descriptivist movement's lasting contribution was not a new set of grammar rules but a new way of asking questions about language. Instead of asking "Is this correct?" the Descriptivists taught scholars to ask "Does this communicate effectively, and why?" This shift in questioning was [______] — it did not eliminate standards but relocated them from authority to evidence.`,
