      explanation: `The sentence describes what the shift in questioning was — a shift from authority-based to evidence-based standards. The word must precisely characterize the nature of this shift. The passage specifies: it "did not eliminate standards but relocated them." This is not just a large change (significant, important) or an extreme change (radical); it is a change that fundamentally transformed how the enterprise worked — a change in the underlying framework. Option B, "transformative," precisely captures this: a transformative change is one that changes the nature or structure of something, not just its degree. Option A, "significant," means notable or large in scale but does not describe the fundamental restructuring. Option C, "important," is even vaguer. Option D, "radical," means extreme or going to the root — and while the shift was foundational, "radical" typically implies more aggressive or disruptive change than a careful "relocation" of standards implies; "transformative" is more precise for a change that fundamentally restructured an existing practice rather than overthrowing it.`,
